oding proteolipid protein (PLP).","claim":"PLP1 causes Pelizaeus-Merzbacher disease","claim_id":"c_f3be7cde2d79","predicate":"causes","polarity":"supports","study_context":"not_stated","model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","prompt_version":"extract-7c36af1f"},{"db":"PubMed","origin":"Claude extract","record":"PMID:41736546","url":"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/41736546/","level":"text_mined","date":"2026-02-01","confidence":0.7,"snippet":"Oligodendrocytes (OLs), the myelinating cells of the central nervous system, are particularly prone to pathogenic G-to-A mutations, such as PLP1A243V, which causes Pelizaeus-Merzbacher disease (PMD), a lethal hypomyelinating disorder lacking effective therapy.","claim":"PLP1 causes Pelizaeus-Merzbacher disease","claim_id":"c_26fece833056","predicate":"causes","polarity":"supports","study_context":"not_stated","model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","prompt_version":"extract-7c36af1f"},{"db":"PubMed","origin":"Claude extract","record":"PMID:42378126","url":"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/42378126/","level":"text_mined","date":"2026-06-01","confidence":0.7,"snippet":"Mutations in the PLP1 gene cause various X-linked hereditary spastic paraplegias phenotypes, including Pelizaeus-Merzbacher disease and spastic paraplegia type 2.","claim":"PLP1 causes Pelizaeus-Merzbacher disease","claim_id":"c_463afeed1fd8","predicate":"causes","polarity":"supports","study_context":"not_stated","model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","prompt_version":"extract-7c36af1f"},{"db":"PubMed","origin":"Claude extract","record":"PMID:39322379","url":"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/39322379/","level":"text_mined","date":"2024-01-01","confidence":0.7,"snippet":"PLP1-related disorders are caused by hemizygous pathogenic variants in the proteolipid protein 1 (PLP1) gene, and encompass classic Pelizaeus-Merzbacher disease, the severe connatal form, PLP1-null syndrome, spastic paraplegia type 2, and hypomyelination of early myelinating structures.","claim":"PLP1 causes Pelizaeus-Merzbacher diseas